      per source attempt: 1 application write + 4 reserved private/mirror writes; <= 2 whole-parent puts (old/new groups); all share the 1024-row mutation ceiling
      composed mutation: <= 204 such source transitions, <= 408 parent puts; other writes and meters can lower this bound
      posts.likeCount: <= 16417 B per parent put, including event framing; private total emits 0 B; mirror preserves other fields and maintains every parent index
      own derived stream bytes: <= 6698136 B per composed mutation, per recipient (application events, acknowledgements and reply envelope excluded)
      activation: private rebuild + in-place mirror, 0 row-event bytes; parent barrier always commits; device reacquires, no column prediction
      schema bounds may exceed 16777216 B; no write-time byte guard; an oversized current-generation stream at limit 1 restarts by snapshot with pending writes preserved
